-39, 57, 128, 128 10000 -> (−39, 57, 128, 128) are the four largest circles of their gasket. Its numbers leave 0, 8, 9, 12, 17, 20 on division by 24. By the paper’s theorem no number in it is three times a square or six times a square. In a gasket with these remainders either the fourth powers and 4 times a fourth power are ruled out, or 9 and 36 times a fourth power are. The page finds which by looking for one of them on a circle, and up to 10,000 it finds none. Going through its 544 circles with a number up to 10,000: 2,231 numbers that pass the test are missing, 48 of them in the families ruled out (marked with an orange square) and 2,183 not.
