-39, 57, 128, 128 100000 -> (−39, 57, 128, 128) are the four largest circles of their gasket. Its numbers leave 0, 8, 9, 12, 17, 20 on division by 24. By the paper’s theorem no number in it is three times a square or six times a square. In this gasket 9 times and 36 times a fourth power are ruled out as well. The page finds that by looking: 50,625 is on a circle, and 50,625 = 15 × 15 × 15 × 15; and in a gasket with these remainders either the fourth powers and 4 times a fourth power are ruled out, or 9 and 36 times a fourth power are. Going through its 10,984 circles with a number up to 100,000: 20,049 numbers that pass the test are missing, 172 of them in the families ruled out (marked with an orange square) and 19,877 not.
